Mall of America in 
Bloomington, Minnesota. The opening of each new store is celebrated with a weekend-long event in which a Master Model Builder creates, with the help of volunteers—most of whom are children
[examples needed]—a larger-than-life Lego statue, which is then displayed at the new store for several weeks.
